  "Number": 44,
  "Question": "If \\(x\\lt a\\lt0\\) means that \\(x\\) and \\(a\\) are numbers such that \\(x\\) is less than \\(a\\) and \\(a\\) is less than zero, then:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(x^2\\lt ax\\lt0\\)",
    "B": "\\(x^2\\gt ax\\gt a^2\\)",
    "C": "\\(x^2\\lt a^2\\lt0\\)",
    "D": "\\(x^2\\gt ax\\) but \\(ax\\lt0\\)",
    "E": "\\(x^2\\gt a^2\\) but \\(a^2\\lt0\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Because \\(x<a<0\\), both \\(x\\) and \\(a\\) are negative. Multiplication by a negative number reverses an inequality.\n\nMultiplying \\(x<a\\) by \\(x\\) gives\n\\[\nx^2>ax.\n\\]\nMultiplying the same inequality by \\(a\\) gives\n\\[\nax>a^2.\n\\]\nCombining these, we obtain \\(\\boxed{x^2>ax>a^2}\\). Also, \\(a^2>0\\), so all three quantities are positive. The answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
